  "prefLabel": "Tax 210.07 Comparables",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Tax 210.07 Comparables. Except by board leave, parties shall be limited to no more than 10 comparables per residential property and 20 comparables per nonresidential property. Parties may move for leave, at least 4 weeks prior to the hearing, to use more comparables, and the board shall grant the motion if the moving party has shown the additional comparables are necessary to the party’s case and will not be unduly repetitious or burdensome on the board or the other party.\n\nSource. #5638, eff 9-1-93; ss by #7068, INTERIM, eff 8-15-99, EXPIRES, 12-13-99; ss by #7153, eff 12-10-99; ss by #7874-B, eff 4-18-03; ss by #8987-A, eff 9-24-07; ss by #9538, eff 9-8-09; ss by #10625-B,eff 6-26-14; ss by #13711-B, eff 8-2-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/tax100-500.html"
